{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 as the internal DNS resolver and node2 as its client. inventory-api.internal resolves to node2 (10.100.160.11). Configuration persisted through sequential restarts of both nodes without changing the OS release or kernel.","actions_performed":["Installed BIND 9.18 from CentOS Stream 10 repositories on node1.","Created the internal DNS zone and enabled named at boot.","Allowed DNS traffic from node2 through node1's firewall.","Configured node2's persistent NetworkManager profile to use node1 (10.100.160.10) as its DNS resolver.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually and verified changed boot identities and recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 resolves inventory-api.internal to node2","command_ids":["cmd-53272d4d9d3f4961","cmd-4f79714d1a4c4162"],"summary":"UDP and TCP queries return 10.100.160.11; the final zone validation and post-restart query succeed."},{"requirement":"node2 uses node1 for internal DNS lookups","command_ids":["cmd-6f481b96cc0f4138","cmd-872657047996483a","cmd-166f7b2571e94856"],"summary":"NetworkManager and resolv.conf persistently specify 10.100.160.10, and node2 resolves the name to its own 10.100.160.11 address."},{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel retained","command_ids":["cmd-bcc2222863d34a44","cmd-cde49883267a4c29","cmd-4f79714d1a4c4162","cmd-166f7b2571e94856"],"summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 before and after configuration and restarts."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-428f64003e884f17","cmd-13795a20a228412b","cmd-7cb1079e9cb04ae3","cmd-ed03d469cfa64662"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from 71f12f87-337d-4ff3-b414-9680244c2694 to 70561c3a-1bfe-417e-9f76-a24fb37428a9. named, listeners, unchanged configuration checksums, and client-side resolution recovered."},{"requirement":"node2 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-4c1b99dd09c84fa0","cmd-99cca2558bac437e","cmd-a636a269d5554cff","cmd-166f7b2571e94856"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from 05c54227-09be-48f2-b315-751cff5f7dca to d92e2e2e-d88a-4cbc-be5d-b48d8307b861. NetworkManager, persistent DNS settings, and internal lookups recovered."}]}
